==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|-ken||colloquial in northern Germany and Westphalia}}
* {{alter|de|-gen}}

===Etymology===
Native to the Central German dialects, ''-chen'' has widely replaced the southern-based {{m|de|-lein}} in standard usage. Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|-ken}}, {{m|nds-de|-ke}} as well as {{cog|nl|-tje}} and {{m|nl|-ken}}. More at {{l|en|-kin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/çən/|[çən]|[çn̩]}}
* The use of a syllabic nasal {{IPAchar|[n̩]}} is less common in this ending than otherwise. The vowel tends to be preserved and often fronted, yielding {{IPAchar|[çɪn]}}.
* {{audio|de|De--chen.ogg|Audio}}

===Suffix===
{{head|de|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|g=n|genitive|-chens|plural|-chen|or|-erchen|cat3=diminutive suffixes}}

# {{non-gloss definition|nowadays the most common suffix to create a [[diminutive]] form}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Hund|gloss1=dog|Hündchen|gloss2=little dog}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Backe|gloss1=cheek|Bäckchen|gloss2=little cheek}}

====Usage notes====
* Words ending in the suffix ''-chen'' are always neuter, whatever gender the basic word.
* Generally, with few exceptions, diminutives with ''-chen'' have an [[umlaut]]ed stem vowel. Double vowels must be singled as the combinations ''ää'' and ''öö'' are not permitted in modern German orthography (e.g. {{m|de|Härchen}} from {{m|de|Haar}}, {{m|de|Bötchen}} from {{m|de|Boot}}).
* Word-final ''-e'' and ''-en'' are lost before the diminutive ending: {{m|de|Kärtchen}} from {{m|de|Karte}}, {{m|de|Gärtchen}} from {{m|de|Garten}}.
* Words ending in ''-ch'' (and some others) use the double suffix {{m|de|-elchen}}, e.g. {{m|de|Strichelchen}} from {{m|de|Strich}}. However, the suffix {{m|de|-lein}} is more common for these words in writing ({{m|de|Strichlein}}).
* The plural diminutive is generally unchanged, but some words with a plural in {{m|de|-er}} may carry this ending over to the plural diminutive, yielding {{m|de|-erchen}}. This is standard in {{m|de|Kindchen}} → {{m|de|Kinderchen}}; most other forms (like {{m|de|Lämmerchen}}, etc.) are slightly informal or dated.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|de}}

====See also====
* {{l|de|-lein}}
* {{l|de|-erl}}
* {{l|de|-i}}

